  "judge_reasoning": "## Evaluation\n\n**Task:** Compute the integral of 3e^(2x) from x=0 to x=5.\n\n**Analysis of the screenshots:**\n\n1. **Screenshot 1:** Wolfram Alpha homepage with an empty input field — initial state.\n2. **Screenshot 2:** The query \"integral of 3e^(2x) dx from x=0 to x=5\" has been entered into the Wolfram Alpha search box, correctly formulating the task.\n3. **Screenshot 3:** The results page displays the \"Definite integral\" pod showing:\n   - ∫₀⁵ 3e^(2x) dx = (3/2)(e^10 − 1) ≈ 33038\n   - Also shows the indefinite integral: ∫3e^(2x) dx = (3e^(2x))/2 + constant\n4. **Screenshots 4–5:** Additional result details including the visual representation of the integral (plot) and Riemann sums, confirming the computation was fully rendered.\n\n**Verification of correctness:**\n\nMathematically: ∫₀⁵ 3e^(2x) dx = (3/2)e^(2x) |₀⁵ = (3/2)(e^10 − 1) ≈ (3/2)(22026.47 − 1) ≈ 33038.2\n\nThis matches both the Wolfram Alpha result shown in the screenshot (≈ 33038) and the value stated in the result response (≈ 33038.2). The response is consistent with the screenshot — the slight difference (33038 vs. 33038.2) is just a rounding presentation, not a contradiction.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe integral was correctly computed using Wolfram Alpha, the exact form (3/2)(e^10 − 1) and the numerical approximation were both obtained and reported, and everything aligns with the screenshots.\n\n**Verdict: SUCCESS**",
